{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have strong leads. Let me verify the key facts:\n\n1. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria (d38, d59)\n2. \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages (d38)\n3. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (The Testaments) and Bernardine Evaristo (Girl, Woman, Other) (d50, d53)\n\nBut the question says Book B \"had been released the preceding year\" relative to the year Book A was published. If Book A (An Orchestra of Minorities) was published in 2019, then Book B should have been released in 2018. But The Testaments and Girl, Woman, Other were both published in 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe Book A is \"The Fishermen\" (2015), and the 2015 Booker Prize winner is the relevant one. Let me check the 2015 Booker Prize winner and whether The Fishermen was translated into 25+ languages.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Booker Prize 2015 winner A Brief History of Seven Killings Marlon James\", \"The Fishermen Chigozie Obioma 2015 Booker shortlist translated languages\", \"Marlon James born birthplace city\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_f9747ad8252c4eb5ae3a73fd","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d38\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_eff7df42204b484ba21c860a","index":1,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789460477,"id":"chatcmpl-d7168b7e-50c4-9471-b730-8f01f6ac0032","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":21059,"completion_tokens":299,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":21358,"cached_tokens":11392,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":11392},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}